{"term":"recycle","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6b25fec2e16d22f60b","definition":"To break down and reuse component materials.","example":"Both paper and plastic can be recycled.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["ecycle","Freecycle","freecycle","grasscycle","recyclability","recyclable","recyclate","recycle bin","recyclebot","recycle day","recycle man","recycle shop","recycle time","recycle truck","recyclic","recycling","recyclist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recycle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:0f9583bba2e06aa7a4","definition":"To reuse as a whole.","example":"Jokes are recycled so frequently, it’s as if comedy writing was eating a hole in the ozone layer: If the audience had a nickel for every time a character on one side of the frame says something could never happen as it simultaneously happens on the other side of the frame, they’d have enough to pay the surcharge for the movie’s badly implemented 3-D.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, transitive","wordFamily":["ecycle","Freecycle","freecycle","grasscycle","recyclability","recyclable","recyclate","recycle bin","recyclebot","recycle day","recycle man","recycle shop","recycle time","recycle truck","recyclic","recycling","recyclist"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recycle#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:106bc7fe6f53e562dd","definition":"To collect or place in a bin for recycling.","example":"Most cans, bottles, and jars need to be rinsed, so recycle while you are doing dishes.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive, transitive","wordFamily":["ecycle","Freecycle","freec